re testing whether drones can help firefighting crews respond more quickly to small fires and put them out before they become more destructive. The California Department of Forestry and Fire Protection, also known as CAL FIRE, ran its own field test involving five autonomous drones that worked together to deploy between 500 and 1,000 gallons of foam combined for suppressing fires on July 15, according to the TV station KPMH . The demonstration was organized with the help of the nonprofit FireWERX and the California-based company Seneca , which is making the drones commercially available starting in 2026. Read full article Commentsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;UJaK04zgf59kUzAw85BmKn7GyhbjsEdelLKReo9FnRkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;szjUJGJ4o4E5h7fvqmMOIuie3sKT8kFluL37nt5Sfwoƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;uof04R_k-7f4HwEDuyBqfEtD91_VlIs-TpJ7EWSky0gƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;K-R8geyqdMmtifVQ1WSSiWDcjlMpBMnLKkKiFrNmb9Eƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;LXeWGrGu5R0UMv7whUBOUUDTEHJKaz4tAypOYjJrcXQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Wl9EHKMIWeKPXAEvOmj8T0kQBcOIo2-jgaTtfP9pFKMƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bX8deSasBHaBaQ_2idksnRV_bd3KHO3_GK2EtJ1Z9NAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Fo3F01rkckIebWAm2X2rhunDeSeYjWvYmxXkkIDA6Loƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightduni